claims:
1. A data processing apparatus comprising:
 an interface configured to couple to one or more memory channels of a system memory;
a local memory;
execute circuitry; and
access circuitry to:
receive data access instructions to access the system memory that have corresponding execute instructions that were received by the execute circuitry;
exchange synchronization information with the execute circuitry to store data obtained from the system memory to the local memory for the execute circuitry to use for one or more compute iterations; and
cause data access operations to access the system memory through the interface to obtain the data based on the received data access instructions and the exchanged synchronization information, wherein a low-latency memory access is enabled by storing data to the local memory during the data access operations for the execute circuitry to compute results in the one or more compute iterations using the data stored to the local memory.

21. A system comprising:
a system memory; and
a data processing device to include;
an interface configured to couple to the system memory through one or more memory channels;
a local memory;
execute circuitry; and
access circuitry to:
receive data access instructions to access the system memory that have corresponding execute instructions that were received by the execute circuitry;
exchange synchronization information with the execute circuitry to store data obtained from the system memory to the local memory in order for the execute circuitry to use the data for one or more compute iterations without waiting for the data to be stored to the local memory; and
cause data access operations to access the system memory through the interface to obtain the data based on the received data access instructions and the exchanged synchronization information.
